    skos:definition "In Commerce, the grains of several species of *gramina*. Those of most importance are clover seed, flax or linseed, hemp seed, rape seed, tares, mustard seed &c.; for which, see the respective articles. [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1352]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (processing_state=raw_unprocessed): Processing state: whole nuts/kernels/seeds/peas are unprocessed; classifier matched 'expressing Oil', 'Ground (nuts)' or 'Split'. Layer-1 observations: 126 rows, 1856–1906. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×126. Units: Qrs. (Quarters) ×126. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×11; Russia → United Kingdom ×8; Germany → United Kingdom ×8; British India Madras → United Kingdom ×6."@en, "Curated fields — definition excerpt: Definition ran on into the next entries (SEGARS, SENNA)."@en ;
